  root_module.f90
      Bracketed-interval root solver library from the roots-fortran
      project by Jacob Williams
      (https://github.com/jacobwilliams/roots-fortran). The `zero_uh2p`
      function in uh_optim.f90 invokes the `brent` solver from this
      module `root_scalar(method, fun, ax, bx, ...)`. Copyright (c) 
      2021-2025 Jacob Williams.

      Local modifications vs upstream:
        (1) File renamed from root_module.F90 (capital F = preprocessed)
            to root_module.f90 and the C-preprocessor conditionals that
            select the real kind (REAL32/REAL64/REAL128) were resolved
            to the default real64 branch, so the file compiles with R's
            standard Makeconf suffix rules.
        (2) The nested helper `isign` inside the toms748 solver was
            renamed to `rf_isign` to avoid shadowing the Fortran
            intrinsic `isign` (CRAN -Wintrinsic-shadow warning).
